{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1248782-players-in-the-southern-wyld","id":1248782,"title":"players in the southern wyld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-22T15:59:28-07:00","id":1248782,"title":"players in the southern wyld","content":"I'll soon be having a circle of players going into the wyld, in search of ancient lost Dragon King cities - they're looking for dirt on the Varang (its a 2.5 game)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm planning to have them bump into at least one fair folk court - but I'm a little unsure of how to play to 'environmentals' - when they reach the deep wyld and whatnot.<br /> <br /> They're coming in from the south-east - south of the Varang city states - heading into the wyld. They have a very old rough map (from the time of the Baloran crusades) trailing the route of a chronicler who was running from the encroaching wyld.<br /> <br /> I'm just a bit for a loss of how to describe the near-chaos they'll be venturing out to. I'm thinking stuff like &quot;Jungles with foliage of fire&quot;, &quot;crustal deserts&quot;, &quot;living sand&quot; but I feel I need more... especially for the fair folk court I'm planning on running them by. I am drawing a blank on how to style that place up, or the fair folk there for that matter<br /> <br /> any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T13:32:29-07:00","id":1248886,"title":"","content":"Southern Fae tend to take the forms of Lions, so having them wandering a savannah like region, maybe see lions lounging off in the distance and, if they check, occasional stalks of grass made of glass and diamond. If they keep looking for the Fae, more and more grass becomes made of glass, the ground becomes more sandy underneath, and the lions turn black and become larger. Eventually they find something akin to Pride Rock, but carved from a single diamond under a sky full of fire in all colors, with glass birds doing things for the black lion Fae lounging there, some of whom are fully in lion shape, some who are entirely human save for their lion heads, and some who bear other lion traits. <br /> <br /> That will probably suffice for Bordermarches, maybe light middlemarches. They honestly probably don't want to go further out than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}